# Keep every page under /teddy-riley/ out of Google (and other search engines).
#
# This sends the header rather than disallowing the path in robots.txt on
# purpose: if the path were disallowed, a crawler could never fetch a page to
# see this header (or a <meta noindex> tag), and a URL discovered some other
# way — a link from outside, someone sharing it — could still turn up in
# search results with no title or description. Allowing the crawl but
# tagging every response noindex is what actually keeps it out. See
# https://developers.google.com/search/docs/crawling-indexing/block-indexing
#
# Confirmed mod_headers works on this host: the blog root's .htaccess already
# sets security headers this way and they show up on the live site.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header set X-Robots-Tag "noindex, nofollow"
</IfModule>
